@inherits LayoutComponentBase
@inject AuthService Auth
@inject IJSRuntime JS

@*
    The layout outside the signed-in app: sign-in, set-password, forgot-password, the connector's
    consent page, the Imagine viewer. It draws NOTHING until the sign-in check has answered —
    the boot overlay stays up over an empty shell — because sign-in has three states, not two,
    and a login page drawn while the answer is still "checking" is the login page flashing at a
    signed-in user before the app jumps to their dashboard (2026-09-16). A page that turns out to
    be a bounce (Login for a signed-in visitor) holds the overlay through its redirect.
*@

<div class="min-h-dvh bg-canvas text-content antialiased">
    @* Sign-in, set-password and forgot-password get the same error surface as the rest of the app:
       a failure here is exactly the kind a user needs to be able to forward. *@
    <ErrorToast />
    @* Sign-in gets the update prompt too: a stale cached bundle on the landing page is exactly
       what makes "sign-in is broken" reports out of a deploy that changed the auth flow. *@
    <UpdateToast />
    @if (Auth.SignIn != SignInState.Checking)
    {
        @Body
    }
</div>

@code {
    protected override Task OnInitializedAsync() => Auth.EnsureInitialisedAsync();

    protected override async Task OnAfterRenderAsync(bool firstRender)
    {
        if (Auth.SignIn != SignInState.Checking) await BootScreen.DismissUnlessHeldAsync(JS);
    }
}
